           service offering for a fee; or
       (c) selling, licensing, sublicensing, renting, or distributing the
           Software or a Derivative Work, as a standalone product or as a
           primary component of a product, in exchange for a fee.

     For the avoidance of doubt, using the Software to operate Your own
     business, including to sell goods or services that are not themselves the
     Software's functionality (for example, running a shop's point of sale, or
     a seller's own live-commerce operations), is NOT Commercial Use unless
     paragraph (a) applies.

1.11 "Annual Gross Revenue" means the total worldwide gross revenue of the
     legal entity exercising rights under this License, aggregated with all
     entities that control, are controlled by, or are under common control
     with it, during the most recent completed twelve-month fiscal period.
     For an individual, it means that individual's total gross income from all
     trade or business activity over the same period.

1.12 "Closed System" means a product, service, platform, or system that does
     any of the following:
       (a) implements a remote kill switch, or requires continuous third-party
           server authorization, for the basic operation of a device or of
           software the user already owns or has licensed, where that
           authorization can be withheld or revoked without the user's
           consent and without a documented, self-serviceable alternative;
       (b) stores the user's own data exclusively in an undocumented
           proprietary format, without providing a documented,
           machine-readable export that the user can invoke at will;
       (c) technically prevents the user from inspecting, modifying, or
           replacing the software running on hardware the user owns;
       (d) collects, monitors, or transmits the user's activity, usage
           patterns, communications, or personal data without prior explicit,
           informed, and independently revocable consent.

     The following do NOT, by themselves, make a product a Closed System:
     ordinary account authentication for a network service the user chooses to
     use; good-faith use of third-party error reporting, crash analytics, or
     product analytics for which a clear, effective opt-out is offered and
     honored; security updates; and license-compliance checks that do not
     disable software the user already lawfully runs.

